        0.5589351251992452
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 13,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "You can stop the channel by writing a 0 into the AUDxEN bit at any time. However, you cannot \nresume the output at the same point in the waveform by just writing a 1 in the bit again. Enabling \nan audio channel almost always starts the data output again from the top of the list of data pointed \nto by the location registers for that channel. If the channel is disabled for a very short time (less \nthan two sampling periods) it may stay on and thus continue from where it left off.\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.76803588867188,
        454.27783203125,
        517.81201171875,
        516.0258178710938
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
